          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "TL 00 NE              REDBOURN             CHERRYTREE LANE                                            (east side) 8 /137                                     Wood End Farmhouse GV                                         II Farmhouse.  C16 or C17 timber frame, cased and extended in red brick later C18.  Plain tile roof.  2 blocks, the W one larger. W block is 2 storeys and attics with dentilled brick eaves.  Its facade is in 2 parts, the left side in chequered brick;  1 sash window with gauged brick lintel to ground and 1st floor;  C20 door.   Right half is plain brick and projects slightly:   C20 window;  1 box dormer;   this part said to have been used as a Quaker meeting hall.   E block is 2 storeys:   chequered brick casing to timber frame;  broad C16/17 red brick chimney stack at far gable end;  2 1st floor casements.  The rear elevation to the farmhouse has a central lateral C17 chimney stack with a tall cruciform stack. Listing NGR: TL0865009762"
    }
  ],
